---
description: Patterns for developing the reference module (formerly salvageunion-reference package)
globs:
  - 'src/reference/**/*.ts'
  - 'tools/**/*.ts'
alwaysApply: false
---

Patterns for developing the reference module with code generation.

- Module structure: `src/reference/` for TypeScript files, `src/reference/data/` for JSON data files, `src/reference/schemas/` for JSON Schema files, `tools/` for code generation scripts
- Always run generation after schema/data changes: `bun run generate`
- NEVER manually edit auto-generated files: `src/reference/utilities-generated.ts`, `src/reference/types/schemas.ts`, `src/reference/types/enums.ts`, `src/reference/types/common.ts`, `src/reference/types/objects.ts`, `src/reference/types/index.ts`, `src/reference/index.ts` (generated from template files)
- To modify generated code: edit generator scripts in `tools/` directory or template files, then run `bun run generate`
- Manual overrides: `src/reference/utilities.ts`, `src/reference/ModelFactory.ts`, `src/reference/BaseModel.ts` (not generated)
- All models extend `BaseModel<T>`, created via `ModelFactory`, use `SalvageUnionReference` static properties to access models, models provide: `all()`, `find()`, `findAll()` methods
- Tests use Bun's built-in test runner: test files `*.test.ts`, run tests with `bun test`, tests validate schema compliance and data integrity
- Build process: Generate (`bun run generate`), Type Check (`bun run typecheck`), Test (`bun test`), Format/Lint, full build: `bun run build`
- All data files must match their JSON schemas, use `tools/validateGenerated.ts` to check generated code, use `tools/validateReferences.ts` to check cross-references
- Adding new data: Add JSON file to `src/reference/data/` directory, add corresponding schema to `src/reference/schemas/` directory, update `tools/schemaNameMap.ts` if needed, run `bun run generate`, run `bun test` to verify
- Using the module: `import { SalvageUnionReference, type SURefChassis } from '../reference'; const chassis = SalvageUnionReference.Chassis.find((c) => c.id === 'some-id')`
